ana_customer: hitting sporadic parse errors in TS streaming json_mode. Started after enabling structured responses. Error is `Unexpected token ',' in JSON at position ...` and seems to coincide with an auth refresh (401 -> refresh -> retry).
maya_support: thanks — can you paste the raw event stream and the ts-sdk version? request id + timestamps help.
ana_customer: oops, typo — here's the raw stream (redacted) and sdk version. sdk: ts-sdk@1.4.2, request id=req_84b9f. raw frames below:

```
data: {"event":"chunk","payload":"{\"reply\": {\"id\":\"r1\",\"text\":\"Hello\""}
data: {"event":"chunk","payload":"\", \"meta\": {\"t\":123}}"}
data: {"event":"end","payload":"},"}  <-- trailing comma fragment
```

maya_support: that last end payload looks like it injects a trailing comma. does your app show any auth/retry logs around the same time?

ana_customer: yes — logs show a 401 then immediate refresh then a retry: 

```
2026-03-15T12:34:55Z INFO request id=req_84b9f token_expired
2026-03-15T12:34:56Z INFO auth refresh success new_token=***
2026-03-15T12:34:56Z INFO retrying request id=req_84b9f attempt=2
2026-03-15T12:34:57Z ERROR parser Unexpected token , at position 342
```

tony_eng: thanks for the repro. hypothesizing: our serializer emits a separator (`,`) between top-level objects. on normal single-stream it's fine, but if a retry/abort interleaves an extra end frame we may end up writing an additional ",". looks like the `end` frame payload is `},` which leaves a trailing comma when concatenated with previous payloads.

ryan_ts: can you try a minimal repro locally? set `DEBUG=ts-sdk:stream` and run this node snippet to simulate a retry + chunk boundary: 

```js
// repro.js (node)
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
(async () => {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/stream?json_mode=true', { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer INVALID' } });
  // sdk will refresh and retry automatically in this env; inspect raw body
  res.body.on('data', chunk => process.stdout.write(chunk));
})();
```

Also set env `TS_SDK_SIMULATE_AUTH_REFRESH=1` (we've added a flag to simulate in recent builds). if you can reproduce, dump the raw chunks to a file and attach.

maya_support: escalating to eng-runtime with tags `jsonmode`, `ts-sdk`, `auth-retry`, `streaming-parse`. tagging @tony_eng @ryan_ts.

tony_eng: looks actionable. root cause candidate: double-separator on end+retry. plan: change serializer to avoid emitting a separator if the next frame is `end` or if `end` already includes a closing bracket. add unit test for interleaved retry boundary and add a defensive parser on the client to ignore solitary trailing separators. i'll open a PR and assign RNF-5123. ETA: EOD for patch and tests.

ana_customer: thanks — temporary workaround that helped was overriding `streamingJsonSeparator: '\n'` in the client config so the parser tolerates the trailing comma. not ideal but reduces failures.

ci-bot: created issue RNF-5123 and linked reproduction artifacts (uploaded repro.log). assigned to tony_eng. https://tracker.redwood.ai/RNF-5123

maya_support: we'll follow up here when the patch lands. appreciate the quick repro and logs — will ask for a canary build once ready. :thumbsup:
